+## Amendment, 2026-10-02: endpoint 2 and a fresh M4 ensemble
+
+**DRAFT: not frozen and not in force.** Its pre-freeze review (`experiments/m4/endpoint-2-amendment-review.json`) found an undisclosed predecessor, `experiments/amendments/2026-09-29-m4-growth.md`, and the user must decide how to proceed. Until this line is removed and the amended file's hash is added to `experiments/FROZEN`, nothing below applies.
+
+Written after the 2026-09-28 M4 ensemble was analysed, and decided by the user on 2026-10-02. The original text above, including endpoint 2, is unchanged and still computed. This amendment applies only to a fresh ensemble; the 2026-09-28 ensemble keeps its verdict and is never re-read under it.
+
+**Why.** M4 failed on endpoint 2. Treatment runs were "growing" (20/20 on `gradient-m3`, 8/10 on `spots-m3`), but so were all 30 neutral runs, and endpoint 2 requires at most a minority. This is structural (exploratory reasoning, recorded in `docs/plan.md`):
+- neutral runs express the reference phenotype, but mutation still mints lineage labels at a steady rate;
+- the frozen threshold is the neutral pilot's 95th percentile of lineage activity, so about 5% of neutral lineages cross it;
+- neutral cumulative new activity therefore rises almost linearly and is classified "growing", whatever treatment does.
+
+**Amended endpoint 2: late-window excess activity** (`late-excess-activity`; `AMENDMENT_2026_10_02` in `experiments/endpoints.ts`, executed by `tools/analyze.ts`).
+- **Per-run statistic:** the rate of new evolutionary activity in the second half of the registered window. It is cumulative new activity at the final census minus its value at the last census at or before half the horizon, per 10⁵ steps. Activity uses endpoint 1's frozen per-preset threshold, unchanged.
+- **Hypothesis:** treatment > neutral, one-sided exact Mann–Whitney, α = 0.01.
+- **Reading:** treatment is still producing adaptively significant lineages faster than the neutral shadow in the second half of the window.
+- **What it cannot show:** it measures excess over neutral, not unboundedness. Within a finite window it cannot tell a real treatment effect that saturates more slowly than the window from open-ended growth. Results remain "practical open-endedness over the observation window" at most, as declared above.
+- **Original endpoint 2** is still computed and reported, labelled "original; superseded for the M4 gate by the 2026-10-02 amendment".
+
+**Null calibration** (`tools/nullcal.ts`, window 10⁶, 32 replicates, 20 seeds per condition; `runs/nullcal/amendment-2026-10-02`):
+- The amended endpoint passes 0/32 on `longPeriodLoop`, `neutralDrift` and `randomWalkNoise`, and 1/32 on `saturatingProcess`. Pooled over the four exchangeable nulls that is 1/128, with 95% interval [0.0002, 0.043], consistent with α = 0.01.
+- `neutralDrift` is nearly uninformative for this endpoint, because its lineages fix early and few cross the threshold late. `randomWalkNoise` is the informative null.
+- The bounded-treatment scenario (`boundedTreatmentVsFlat`) passes 32/32, as does the amended gate. This shows the specificity limit stated above. The original endpoint 2 rejected that scenario only because its neutral runs were also "growing".
+- The original rows reproduce the plan's recorded 10⁶ results exactly.
+
+**M4 gate (amended).** M4 is met when endpoint 1 and amended endpoint 2 both hold in the fresh ensemble, on both `gradient-m3` and `spots-m3`. `tools/analyze.ts` reports the gate per preset.
+
+**Fresh ensemble:**
+- presets `gradient-m3` and `spots-m3`, the M3 founder set, and RULE_VERSION 1;
+- 10⁶ steps, census every 100, deep every 10, with the frozen activity thresholds (presets unchanged, so their identities still match);
+- conditions treatment, neutral and no-mutation;
+- seeds 21–40 per condition on both presets, giving 120 runs. `spots-m3` rises from 10 to 20 seeds. This is fixed before any new data, because endpoint 1 missed there at p = 0.0116 with 10 seeds.
+- These seeds are disjoint from the M4 ensemble (1–20), the calibration pilot (1001–1020) and the registered extension (101–105, 1101–1110).
+- `tools/analyze.ts` evaluates the amended endpoint only for an ensemble whose every seed lies in 21–40, or for a synthetic calibration. For any other ensemble it does not compute the statistic.
+- **Other endpoints:** endpoint 3 cannot be tested, since it needs the replenished control. Endpoint 4 and whichever held-out comparisons these conditions allow are reported descriptively; none is confirmatory here.
+
+**Analysis code:** `tools/analyze.ts` at the commit that records this amendment's hash in `experiments/FROZEN`. On synthetic ensembles it reproduces the original endpoints and held-out results byte for byte (`experiments/test/amendment-2026-10-02.test.ts`).
+
+**Launch** needs a separate release fixing the run manifest, budget cap and placement. The user's decision (2026-10-02) is to decide on the launch after the founder-discovery continuation study reports (`experiments/founder-discovery/v1/continuation-protocol.md`).
